<h2 class="bold" id="color"><a class="underline reset-text-decoration" href="tokens#color">Color</a></h2>
<p>Colors are defined as <strong>CSS custom properties</strong> that automatically adapt to light and dark themes. Use CSS variables in your styles instead of fixed color values.</p>
<p><strong>CSS Variables</strong><br/>
<span class="code-wrapper code-container inline" style="background-color:hsl(230, 1%, 98%);color:hsl(230, 8%, 24%)"><code class="code code--inline prism-code language-markup code-inline"><span class="token-line" style="color:hsl(230, 8%, 24%)"><span class="token plain">var(--color-text-default)</span></span></code></span>, <span class="code-wrapper code-container inline" style="background-color:hsl(230, 1%, 98%);color:hsl(230, 8%, 24%)"><code class="code code--inline prism-code language-markup code-inline"><span class="token-line" style="color:hsl(230, 8%, 24%)"><span class="token plain">var(--color-surface-primary)</span></span></code></span>, etc.</p>
<p>Our semantic color tokens automatically adapt based on the <span class="code-wrapper code-container inline" style="background-color:hsl(230, 1%, 98%);color:hsl(230, 8%, 24%)"><code class="code code--inline prism-code language-markup code-inline"><span class="token-line" style="color:hsl(230, 8%, 24%)"><span class="token plain">.is-light</span></span></code></span> or <span class="code-wrapper code-container inline" style="background-color:hsl(230, 1%, 98%);color:hsl(230, 8%, 24%)"><code class="code code--inline prism-code language-markup code-inline"><span class="token-line" style="color:hsl(230, 8%, 24%)"><span class="token plain">.is-dark</span></span></code></span> theme applied to the page. Color names describe their purpose rather than their appearance, enabling flexible theming and maintainability.</p>
